  "headline": "Queen of the Hills",
  "short_description": "Darjeeling is famed for its tea estates, views of Kanchenjunga, and the UNESCO-listed Darjeeling Himalayan Railway.",
  "about": "A former British colonial hill station in the Himalayan foothills, Darjeeling is world-renowned for its tea industry and views toward Kanchenjunga, the world's third-highest peak.\n\nLocated in the Lesser Himalayas of northern West Bengal, at around 2,050 m elevation.\n\nA blend of Nepali, Lepcha, Bhutia and Bengali influences, shaped by its tea-plantation history and Himalayan Buddhist heritage.\n\nA mix of Hindu, Buddhist and Christian communities, reflected in its temples, monasteries and colonial-era churches.",
  "history": "Developed by the British in the 19th century as a sanatorium and hill station, and as the centre of a major tea-growing region.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Bagdogra Airport (airport, ~70 km)\n- New Jalpaiguri (railway)\n- Darjeeling Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Nepali, Bengali, Hindi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "March to May, and October to December",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2–3 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Bagdogra Airport (IXB), ~70 km away",
  "nearest_railway_station": "New Jalpaiguri (NJP), connected onward by the toy train or road",
